\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{The version of WordStar in this archive is \b "WordStar for DOS North American English Version 7.0 Rev. D."\b0   By default, it uses WordStar's American English dictionary and American English thesaurus.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{But I've also supplied additional dictionaries, which you can switch to on the fly from within a document by using the \b .la\b0  command followed by the DOS country-code number for that language (more dictionaries were published, I believe, but I don't have them):}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .la 001  English (US)}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .la 044  English (UK)}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .la 358  Finnish}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .la 002  French (Canada)}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .la 033  French (France)}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .la 049  German}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .la 039  Italian}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .la 052  Spanish (Mexico)}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{ .la 034  Spanish (Spain)}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{If you like, you can included text such as "English (UK)" as part of the dot command as a memory aid, as I have above, but you don't have to: the bare command \b ".la 044"\b0  works just fine.}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{If you want to permanently switch the default language for your dictionary and thesaurus, you can do that easily at \b WSCHANGE\b0  menu \b D\b0 , \b C\b0 , \b G\b0 , \b K\b0  ("Language Default").}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{If you do a spellcheck now by issuing \b ^QL\b0 , you'll see that the\~\b .la\b0  codes below cause the words in various languages to be properly recognized or flagged as misspelling}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{\b US ENGLISH TEST:\b0 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{tire}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0{tyre}\par
